{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560699-v5-discipline-questions","id":1560699,"title":"[V5] Discipline Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-06-18T02:42:39-07:00","id":1560699,"title":"[V5] Discipline Questions","content":"Cutting to the chase or I'll just rumble about how I hate Paradox:<br /> <br /> On Auspex 3: Share the Senses<br /> 1. The book says &quot;kindred or mortal&quot;. Does it work on animals or other supernatural beings? Does it work on a Famulus?<br /> 2. It requires line of sight for a stranger, explicitly not so for someone who ingested your blood, but what about an acquaintance or friend that didn't eat your blood?<br /> 3. Requires a Rouse Check <i>and </i>a roll with Dif 3. Is it right? Isn't a bit over for something so binary?<br /> 4. Says difficulty can go higher depending on several factors, but no reference to even begin imagining where to put it.<br /> <br /> The problem with 2 and 4 is that they talk past each other and on quite objective and recurring factors, the kind that should be clear:<br /> <br /> 5. How far can I try if I have line of sight?<br /> 6. How far can I try if target has my blood?<br /> 7. After all, does knowing the target matter or not?<br /> 8. If the amount of blood matters, as it says it does unambiguously, how so?<br /> 9. Does line of sight include cameras? Powers? Or only direct physical perception?<br /> <br /> For me the simpler reading is that Dif 3 covers either direct line of sight <b><i>or </i></b>a freshly fed Ghoul, and that here line of sight is also line of effect (physical proximity, unaided visual), but that's too ambiguous to be sure. And camera feeds wouldn't be too overpowered for a power that bypass their need if you know the target.<br /> <br /> Is there any further clarification on any of those aspects anywhere in official material? How do you deal with this power at your table?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T14:23:55-07:00","id":1560830,"title":"","content":"Technically, the wording is even worse than that. It says you can use it on &quot;another mortal or Kindred&quot;, which means you can only use it on a mortal if you're also mortal (e.g., a ghoul who's somehow learned a third-level Discipline).<br /> <br /> Based on the assumption the wording is just very lax and not intentionally specific, I would say that &quot;Kindred or mortal&quot; implies humanoid beings. It wouldn't cover animals or a famulus, since those are covered by Animalism. I could maybe be convinced for a famulus, but it's a reach. It probably would work on Garou, mages, etc., since they have human-like minds.<br /> <br /> For range, I'd say it works at any range provided you have LOS with the naked eye. I wouldn't count a camera as providing line of sight because, in a strict sense, you don't have a direct line of sight. But a telescope? You might allow it at higher difficulty, although, again, I think that's a reach. Disciplines don't usually work through technology unless they say they do.<br /> <br /> Without LOS, you need the target to have consumed your blood. When they say &quot;stranger&quot;, they probably mean &quot;non-familiar&quot; (i.e., someone who hasn't drunk your blood recently). A target who's ingested your blood can be targeted anywhere in the world, hence why you don't need LOS, but a friend still requires LOS if they haven't consumed your vitae. You would increase the difficulty if they're far away, but you might reduce it if you know them intimately.<br /> <br /> I put the whole thing down to either a poor translation from someone's native Swedish or whatever, or just slapdash wording in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T15:22:38-07:00","id":1560833,"title":"","content":"Overall agree, but still annoying.<br /> <br /> I would push on one thing: there's an amalgam with Animalism of same level that let's you get the senses of <i>several</i> animals at once. Or so says the Paradox Wiki.<br /> <br /> Confirmed, I'd say it may indicate this is ok for 1on1. But I can't find it in my copy of Fall of London (horribly organized book). I found no power in Animalism to do something similar before <i>Subsume the Spirit, </i>so I'm not sure this should be there.<br /> <br /> My current interpretation is:<br /> 1. Any target (pending decision on animals);<br /> 2. It requires LoS or ingested Blood;<br /> 3. Roll Dif 3 if LoS (and?or?) Blood.<br /> <br /> Remaining problems:<br /> 1. Distance and time since blood feeding, maybe quantity, affect Dif, but no idea how.<br /> 2. LoS sets Dif to minimum or reduces? Unclear.<br /> 3. It's still Rouse + Roll Dif 3. Is this right?<br /> <br /> Curiously it explains what to do in a conflict where another Auspex user is the target better than the base effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-22T04:57:03-07:00","id":1560854,"title":"","content":"Several Disciplines use a rouse check and then a skill test. This is part of why I find rouse checks cumbersome\u2014they should probably be integrated into the activation test instead. But I think it's as intended that you have to do both. I might not require a roll against a mere mortal, though, if their stats were low enough.<br /> <br /> I don't think Auspex powers would typically work on animals at all, and the language mentions &quot;mortals and Kindred&quot;, so that would clearly rule out animals to me. The lack of an equivalent power in Animalism is a problem with Animalism, but I think Subsume the Spirit would be fine and you could create a three-dot Animalism power that provides a lesser version of that effect if you really want it.<br /> <br /> I think the difficulty is 3 if you have either LoS or they have ingested your vitae. Those are required, so you probably can't attempt it at higher difficulty without one or the other of those factors. But the difficulty would rise if the person was particularly far away or they consumed your blood a long time ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T17:01:24-07:00","id":1561094,"title":"","content":"Upon consideration, I reached the following conclusions:<br /> <br /> 1. Agree with you on animals, with a caveat: I would <i><u>house rule</u></i> the <b><i>Famulus </i></b>in as part of the Animalism effect. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5291\" data-vbnamecard=\"5291\">adambeyoncelowe</a> what do you think?<br /> <br /> 2. I don't think Dif should be a concern on most situations, would be too cumbersome, distance should be ok within the same metro area and time ok for a current Ghoul. This would lead to something like that:<br /> - Distance: within county (+0) &gt; state/country (+1) &gt; continent (+2) &gt; planet (+3). A neat Dif 6 to reach anywhere in the world. For this effect I'd rules super countries like Russia, US and Brazil as on continent scope, so the +1 is for a state, oblast or province.<br /> - Time: within Month (+0) &gt; year (+1) &gt; century (+2) &gt; ever (+3).<br /> <br /> Yes, I know it's kinda useful to have it open for the ST to decide. I also know how paralyzing it is for the ST to, having to manage several players with several powers, to be called to adjudicate on the fly without any reference, and I may be overthinking, but this power rubbed me the wrong way in this regard, I'll blame it in the &quot;stranger&quot; wording making me overthinking.<br /> <br /> <b><i>What about the amount of blood?</i></b> This is not an irrelevant matter: tiny amounts do not require a Rouse Check and a drop can go unnoticed in the most inconspicuous things.<br /> <br /> My current character bakes ningy\u014dyaki and other Japanese confectionery as a hobby, and could add drops of blood to the fillings.<br /> <br /> A. Should the amount be noticeable?<br /> <br /> B. Should it require a Rouse Check?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T02:32:50-07:00","id":1561121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560699-v5-discipline-questions?p=1561094#post1561094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Upon consideration, I reached the following conclusions:<br /> <br /> 1. Agree with you on animals, with a caveat: I would <i><u>house rule</u></i> the <b><i>Famulus </i></b>in as part of the Animalism effect. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5291\" data-vbnamecard=\"5291\">adambeyoncelowe</a> what do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean, as part of Animalism's Bond Famulus power, it should specifically let you use things like Auspex's Share the Senses? I think that's more than fine. Someone learning Bond Famulus is essentially bonding their soul with the animal's, so it seems natural to me from that angle.<br /> <br /> The main difference is that this ability comes from knowing the Animalism power rather than the Auspex power, which makes it more on-theme and makes Bond Famulus a bit better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560699-v5-discipline-questions?p=1561094#post1561094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. I don't think Dif should be a concern on most situations, would be too cumbersome, distance should be ok within the same metro area and time ok for a current Ghoul. This would lead to something like that:<br /> - Distance: within county (+0) &gt; state/country (+1) &gt; continent (+2) &gt; planet (+3). A neat Dif 6 to reach anywhere in the world. For this effect I'd rules super countries like Russia, US and Brazil as on continent scope, so the +1 is for a state, oblast or province.<br /> - Time: within Month (+0) &gt; year (+1) &gt; century (+2) &gt; ever (+3).<br /> <br /> Yes, I know it's kinda useful to have it open for the ST to decide. I also know how paralyzing it is for the ST to, having to manage several players with several powers, to be called to adjudicate on the fly without any reference, and I may be overthinking, but this power rubbed me the wrong way in this regard, I'll blame it in the &quot;stranger&quot; wording making me overthinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they probably meant &quot;not a familiar&quot; (in the <i>Blade</i> meaning of the word, as in a ghoul or blood doll). That's the only rational explanation I can think of. But this is reasonable and works well.<br /> <br /> Maybe it would have helped for mechanical purposes if they'd included more standardised wording. Then they'd only need to use a simple term consistently and they could cut a lot of explanations and rules ambiguity.<br /> <br /> E.g., you could have a &quot;blood familiar&quot; (anyone who has tasted your blood), &quot;blood donor&quot; (anyone whose blood <i>you</i> have tasted), and &quot;blood stranger&quot; (someone whose blood you don't know). Then you could have a single set of rules to determine how intense that relationship is\u2014if the blood was tasted more than a month ago, it's +1 Difficulty, more than a year ago is +2 Difficulty, more than a decade ago is +3 Difficulty. Reduce the Difficulty by 1 for a sire/childe/dhampir offspring or if you know them very well. Distance could add a modifier on top of that.<br /> <br /> Your suggestion works much the same, so use that if you comfortable with it. But you might want to steal the &quot;blood familiar&quot; terminology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560699-v5-discipline-questions?p=1561094#post1561094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>What about the amount of blood?</i></b> This is not an irrelevant matter: tiny amounts do not require a Rouse Check and a drop can go unnoticed in the most inconspicuous things.<br /> <br /> My current character bakes ningy\u014dyaki and other Japanese confectionery as a hobby, and could add drops of blood to the fillings.<br /> <br /> A. Should the amount be noticeable?<br /> <br /> B. Should it require a Rouse Check?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were rewriting the rules altogether, I would say:<br /> <br /> A: Since this can be used on pretty much anyone, even those who haven't tasted your vitae, it should be noticeable. This is an optional bonus rather than a core requirement, so there should be a &quot;cost&quot; to that benefit.<br /> <br /> B: Only if you use it on a &quot;blood stranger&quot;. This means anyone who's tasted your blood in the past can be affected without a further rouse check, but it's balanced by them likely noticing the vitae at the time you gave it to them.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, this makes it just a standard power that targets someone you can visualise with a nice bonus for those you're particularly close to/who have tasted your vitae. That seems fair to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":".  CE 06-30-2026, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T05:39:39-07:00","id":1561128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560699-v5-discipline-questions?p=1561121#post1561121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean, as part of Animalism's Bond Famulus power, it should specifically let you use things like Auspex's Share the Senses?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much.<br /> <br /> In my notes I'm putting it in Share the Senses description for convenience, but overall I see Bond Famulus as a very nice &quot;Classic Familiar&quot; vibe that went underused, and is overall weak as the later powers that build on it are later powers.<br /> <br /> Thoroughly agree on the terminology problem. Standardizing technical jargon within the rules goes a long way to make things clear, easy and shorter to write.<br /> <br /> For the amount of blood, I thought to use a compromise where bypassing those increase diff: +1 if you want to either go unnoticed or not require a Rouse Check, +2 for both, +3 to use a live camera feed instead. Not sure if I'll use, but is there as an option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T08:05:44-07:00","id":1561468,"title":"","content":"Seems fair enough to me. Just be mindful of the Difficulty climbing sky-high unexpectedly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}